{"archetypes":[{"name":"enum-placement-drift","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan names a specific insertion point for `cancelled-outline` in render-final-summary.sh using an alphabetical ordering description, but the actual pipe-separated case pattern in that file does not follow strict alphabetical order — a mismatch causes the implementer to insert in the wrong slot, breaking the enum or leaving a gap.","prompt_body":"Read `skills/design/scripts/render-final-summary.sh` line 44 (the pipe-separated outcome case pattern) and compare its actual ordering against the plan's claim that `cancelled-outline` belongs between `cancelled-decompose` and `cancelled-plan-size-hard`. Verify whether the existing sequence is truly alphabetical or follows a different convention, and whether the plan's stated insertion point is consistent with what the file actually contains today. Also check that `SKILL.md` Step 0b's `SUMMARY_OUTCOME` enum list, if present, uses the same ordering convention and that the plan's update instruction matches it. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cancel-invocation-contract","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's cancel-hygiene section for Step 1d.7 says to run the Final summary block with `--post-publish-only` but does not specify the required `--mode` argument that `render-final-summary.sh` demands, which would produce an exit-2 failure at the summary step on every outline-gate cancellation.","prompt_body":"Read `skills/design/scripts/render-final-summary.sh` (specifically its `usage()` function and argument-parsing loop) to confirm which flags are mandatory. Then audit the plan's cancel hygiene specification in the proposed `design-outline.md` contract — does it name all required positional and named arguments (`--outcome`, `--mode`, and any env vars like `DESIGN_TMPDIR`, `SESSION_ID`, `ISSUE_NUMBER`)? Cross-reference at least one existing cancel path in `skills/design/SKILL.md` (e.g., `cancelled-decompose` or `cancelled-brainstorm`) to see what mode value and env state is expected at Step 1d.7. Flag any argument or env-var that the plan omits but the script requires. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"gate-a-residual-reachability","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan reassigns Gate A Shape 1 to Step 1d.7 but must also ensure no existing prose in SKILL.md, approval-gates.md, or brainstorm.md still routes first-time callers directly to Step 1e Gate A Shape 1, which would bypass the new outline-approval gate and leave a ghost entry path.","prompt_body":"Read `skills/design/SKILL.md` (Step 1e block and anti-halt sequence), `skills/design/references/approval-gates.md` (Gate A section), and `skills/design/references/brainstorm.md` (end-of-brainstorm handoff prose) and identify every sentence that directs the orchestrator to Step 1e on a first-time entry path. Determine whether any such direction survives the plan's edits unchanged — specifically, whether the brainstorm.md handoff and the `--trivial`/`--simple`/`--hard` per-tier behavior rows in approval-gates.md still route directly to Step 1e rather than Step 1d.7. Confirm the plan's Step 1e prose update in SKILL.md closes all first-time-entry routes, not just the primary one. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
